 "answer_text": "Found 5 pubmed records, 1 medgen record, 1 literature entity record and 5 clinical trial records for Marfan syndrome [14][15][75][76][77][78][79][80][81][82][83][84]. \n\nMarfan syndrome is a multisystem connective tissue disease with autosomal dominant inheritance caused mainly by FBN1 gene mutation, presenting with diverse clinical manifestations across multiple organ systems [1]. MedGen lists these clinical features: Aortic regurgitation [2], Arachnodactyly [3], Astigmatism [4], Ectopia lentis [5], Esotropia [6], Exotropia [7], Pes planus [8], Glaucoma [9], Congestive heart failure [10], Hypertropia [11] and Micrognathia [12]. \n\nThe Ghent II Nosology criteria are crucial in Marfan syndrome diagnosis, guiding clinicians in identifying high-risk patients [13]. Neonatal Marfan syndrome is especially rare with severe conditions and a poor prognosis [1]. Although no radical treatment method currently exists, early identification, diagnosis, and treatment can effectively prolong patient life span [1]. \n\nPubmed records found\n\nPubmed title: Marfan syndrome [14]. Pubmed title: [Latest advances in the diagnosis and treatment of Marfan syndrome] [77]. Pubmed title: What Is Marfan Syndrome [79]. Pubmed title: Marfan syndrome [81]. Pubmed title: Marfan syndrome [83]. \n\nMedgen records found\n\nMedgen title: Marfan syndrome [15]. \n\nClinical features MedGen lists for Marfan syndrome\n\nMedgen clinical_features: Aortic regurgitation [2]. Medgen clinical_features: Arachnodactyly [3]. Medgen clinical_features: Astigmatism [4]. Medgen clinical_features: Ectopia lentis [5]. Medgen clinical_features: Esotropia [6]. Medgen clinical_features: Exotropia [7]. Medgen clinical_features: Pes planus [8]. Medgen clinical_features: Glaucoma [9]. Medgen clinical_features: Congestive heart failure [10]. Medgen clinical_features: Hypertropia [11]. Medgen clinical_features: Micrognathia [12]. Medgen clinical_features: Mitral regurgitation [16]. Medgen clinical_features: Mitral valve prolapse [17]. Medgen clinical_features: Myopia [18]. Medgen clinical_features: Pneumothorax [19]. Medgen clinical_features: Emphysema [20]. Medgen clinical_features: Retinal detachment [21]. Medgen clinical_features: Retrognathia [22]. Medgen clinical_features: Scoliosis [23]. Medgen clinical_features: Spondylolisthesis [24]. Medgen clinical_features: Strabismus [25]. Medgen clinical_features: Dental crowding [26]. Medgen clinical_features: Tricuspid regurgitation [27]. Medgen clinical_features: Tricuspid valve prolapse [28]. Medgen clinical_features: Cataract [29]. Medgen clinical_features: Bicuspid aortic valve [30]. Medgen clinical_features: Striae distensae [31]. Medgen clinical_features: Pectus carinatum [32]. Medgen clinical_features: Dolichocephaly [33]. Medgen clinical_features: High palate [34]. Medgen clinical_features: Tall stature [35]. Medgen clinical_features: Incisional hernia [36]. Medgen clinical_features: Flexion contracture [37]. Medgen clinical_features: Aortic dissection [38]. Medgen clinical_features: Hypoplasia of the iris [39]. Medgen clinical_features: Protrusio acetabuli [40]. Medgen clinical_features: Downslanted palpebral fissures [41]. Medgen clinical_features: Deeply set eye [42]. Medgen clinical_features: Pulmonary artery dilatation [43]. Medgen clinical_features: Genu recurvatum [44]. Medgen clinical_features: Kyphoscoliosis [45]. Medgen clinical_features: Narrow foot [46]. Medgen clinical_features: Camptodactyly [47]. Medgen clinical_features: Pes cavus [48]. Medgen clinical_features: Ascending tubular aorta aneurysm [49]. Medgen clinical_features: Hammertoe [50]. Medgen clinical_features: Inferior oblique muscle overaction [51]. Medgen clinical_features: Aortic root aneurysm [52]. Medgen clinical_features: Talipes [53]. Medgen clinical_features: Narrow palate [54]. Medgen clinical_features: Microspherophakia [55]. Medgen clinical_features: Increased axial length of the globe [56]. Medgen clinical_features: Premature ost